   "etymology": "Possibly from Proto-Albanian *kśul(V)n, from a regional Proto-Indo-European *kséw-lo-, based on comparison to Ancient Greek ξύλον (xúlon, “timber, beam”) and Proto-Slavic *šulo (“wooden post, pole”). Most support a\nProto-Albanian origin, whereas Orel, on the other hand, considers a South Slavic origin; compare Serbo-Croatian šȗlj (“block of wood”). Beekes considers these cognates, along with possibly Proto-Germanic *sūliz, *sauliz (“beam, post, pillar”), to be ultimately of substrate origin rather than an inherited Indo-European word.",
